  "brief": "a light well / solar chimney that brings daylight down six levels",
  "description": "A heliostat head on the roof - a ring of sun-tracking mirrors around a louvred chimney crown - throws sunlight down a 1.2 m reflective light pipe that runs six levels through the decks inside an open steel frame. A light shelf at every floor spills the light sideways onto the deck; warm air rising in the pipe vents through the crown, pulling fresh air through the floors.",
